            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The invention provides a therapeutic laser system, comprising: a contact cooling element comprising a cooling window configured to directly contact a first skin area of a patient, wherein the cooling window comprises a thermally conductive material that is transmissive to infrared energy; a laser configured to provide a therapeutic laser pulse to a target skin area within the first skin area; a temperature sensor configured to sense a temperature of the target skin area; and a controller configured to: determine that the surface temperature of the target skin area has been cooled from a first surface temperature to a second surface temperature prior to initiating application of a therapeutic laser pulse to the target skin area; initiate the application of a therapeutic laser pulse to the target skin area through the cooling window at a first timepoint, wherein the pulse comprises optical energy having a wavelength within a range of from 1700 nm to 1740 nm, in particular wherein the wavelength is about 1727.5 nm; determine a surface temperature of the target skin area a plurality of times during the application of the therapeutic laser pulse based on infrared energy radiated from the target skin area through the cooling window; and terminate the application of the therapeutic laser pulse to the target skin area at a second timepoint based at least in part on the plurality of surface temperature determinations, wherein each of the plurality of surface temperature determinations occurs during a single therapeutic laser pulse having a pulse duration comprising the period from the first timepoint to the second timepoint.</p>
